[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Read by tenant and channel, the reports hold two
problems with two different outcomes. Each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout>
#4471 closed on 5 October. The parser is fixed. The booking-v3 hint is won't fix: the form is retired.
</Callout>

## What #4471 held

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table counts at render time, the way the desk counts: one id, one report, each report where it
is filed, by tenant and channel.

## The problems

- **`parser`**, [radxhunter/mega-s01e03#1](https://github.com/radxhunter/mega-s01e03/issues/1),
  fixed in `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The shared parser read every date month first,
  and every tenant writes the day first. 7 April became 4 July. Every channel, every tenant.
- **`hint`**, [radxhunter/mega-s01e03#2](https://github.com/radxhunter/mega-s01e03/issues/2),
  won't fix: booking-v3 is retired. Its form printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People typed
  what the hint said, and the form read it the tenant's way, day first. Only the `form` channel of
  booking-v3 tenants. The parser fix did not touch it.
- The reports the desk read as a one-day move are counted under their cause, as the table notes.
  They were filed as [radxhunter/mega-s01e03#3](https://github.com/radxhunter/mega-s01e03/issues/3)
  and closed as a duplicate of #1.

## Why intake missed it

`meta.intakeTag` is a guess from the reporter's browser. The "tagged as" column shows how often
intake filed a report under the other cause.

## Lessons

- A subject line says how a report feels, not what broke. Read the tenant and the channel before you merge.
- One ticket marked known can hold problems with different fixes, and one with no fix at all.

